# Title: Suspicious Binary In User Directory Spawned From Office Application
# ID: aa3a6f94-890e-4e22-b634-ffdfd54792cc
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Jason Lynch
# Date: 2019-04-02
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1204.002, attack.g0046, car.2013-05-002
# Description: Detects an executable in the users directory started from one of the Microsoft Office suite applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Publisher, Visio)
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((parent_process_path="*\\WINWORD.EXE" OR parent_process_path="*\\EXCEL.EXE" OR parent_process_path="*\\POWERPNT.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\MSPUB.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\VISIO.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\MSACCESS.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\EQNEDT32.exe") AND process_path="C:\\users\\*" AND process_path="*.exe") AND NOT ((process_path="*\\Teams.exe")))
